  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 256 PM EDT Mon Oct 12 2026\n\n- Three Chances for Rain This Week, then Cooler\n\nAn area of warm advection/isentropic ascent could bring a few\nshowers and a low chance of thunder tonight, but moisture is\nlimited and most places will remain dry. More rain is possible on\nTuesday night into Wednesday as moisture pools along a stationary\nfront draped across the southern forecast area, but most of the\nprecip should remain to the south.\n\nWidespread rain arrives on Thursday as a shortwave trough digs \nacross the region with a vigorous surface low tracking through the\nGreat Lakes. This is followed by sharply cooler temperatures for\nthe weekend with a widespread freeze expected for Saturday and\nSunday.",
